cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlyFork in your work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "FlyFork: Experimental deterministic branching simulation from a selected Drosophila connectome circuit"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24514875"
identifiers:
  - description: "Concept DOI representing all versions of FlyFork (always resolves to the latest version)"
    type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24514875"
  - description: "Version DOI for FlyFork v0.1.0"
    type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24514876"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gorkemio/flyfork"
url: "https://github.com/gorkemio/flyfork"
abstract: "FlyFork is an open-source browser lab for reproducible, deterministic branching experiments on an 80-neuron DM1 olfactory circuit derived from MaleCNS v1.0 Drosophila connectome data. Users can capture complete simulated states, fork into alternative futures, apply controlled interventions, and verify own-history replay."
authors:
